I don't agree. I think personal pronouns, like demonstratives (ti,
ta, tu) should be evaluated afresh every time they are used, they
shouldn't be bound by a quantifier à la {da}. {le me ma'a moi}
should be "ours" independently of how {ma'a} was used before.

